{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing","id":1516788,"title":"Please someone explain this fiorenza Savona thing...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-30T08:37:51-07:00","id":1516788,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Please someone explain this fiorenza Savona thing...","content":"So let me see if if have this right.<br /> <br /> This apparent ancilla ventrue shows up, talking about how getting MORE involved in the mortal world in the face of the SI is a good idea (no potential negative consequences whatsoever!). And suddenly the whole clan regardless of age is fang-riding her, and theres not so much as a hint of either secret master or directorate intervention, or that shes being set up as the biggest patsy in clan history?<br /> <br /> Being a ventrue antitribu has never seemed a better idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T10:31:13-07:00","id":1516806,"title":"","content":"I would say, it is a bit complex<br /> First, because of her liniage. Savona is the Great-grandchilde of Julia Antasia, making her of Tinia's lineage. Tinia was a respected and feared and quite influental 4th generation ancient, who ruled alongside 13 other vampires over the Etruscans (until she was deposed by her childe Collat) It is told that at the peak of her power, she lost the ability to innovate and began stealing concepts from the best mortal minds.<br /> This is a bit mirrored in her descendants. Julia's political acumen, rhetoric skill, sense of duty, charisma, strong will, common sense, and compassion was quickly cought her sire's attention.<br /> A few unknown vampires later, we reached Savona<br /> She was selected for the value of her contacts, but her sire quickly discovered the quality of her Machiavellian mind, perfectly suited for the Ventrue and the Camarilla. A fresh power player, many elders and ancillae consider her a mere \u201cnew money\u201d Ventrue. Their wiser clanmates know her actions sway councils, corporations, and individual mortals possessing real power. Where her predecessors focused on vampire politics, Fiorenza believes the key to Kindred longevity lies in the manipulation of the living.<br /> And this is another piece of the puzzle<br /> It was not the mortal influance that triggered the Second Inquisition, but the NSA managed to crack SchreckNet and gained firsthand knowledge of the existence of a race of undead bloodsuckers that were spread in all corners of the world. The Vatican, the SO13, the the GRU's Eighth Direction, Israel's Unit 8211, the NSA/CIA Special Access Program called FIRSTLIGHT, France's Calc\u00e9doine.. yes, they harassed numerous vampires, but if you watch their events closely, the SI offed the Tremere of Vienna, the Eighth Direction hunts the Brujah of Russia, Calc\u00e9doine cleared out Marseille, a historically Toreador stronghold, SO13 has systematically cleared London of vampires, but London since the Fall of Mithras wasn't a Ventrue stronghold, no matter what Queen Annne wanted to belive (tho' Mithras played the long Game in his new Monty suit)<br /> The Venture mostly been left alone, and I strongly suspect, especially becasue of the mortal influence Savona and others like her built up. In a sense, she was and is truely the future of the Clan.<br /> Escpecially after the Beconing made the Elders dissapear, most of the Ventrue Elders in theory went away, only a few managed to resist the Call.<br /> These and her powerplay makes her Hardestadt\u200b 2.0 in a sense<br /> <br /> Of course this is my two cents in the matter, but Fiorenza Savona worked hard as a mortal and continues to do so as a Kindred to ensure that wealthy and powerful vampires remain in their positions.<br /> Especially the Ventrue and the ones like her...<br /> As an ascending kingpin of the clan Ventrue, and acting Ventrue Premier of Mexico City? Paired with the web of Boons and her relative young age? In the Beconing-vakuum of Elders and her influence and view of the world?<br /> I think more than enough to &quot;validate her&quot; to be in the position where she is now\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T16:47:45-07:00","id":1516836,"title":"","content":"Not to come off as rude, but we all have access to the same information and copy-pasting the Wiki and books doesn't make it make sense.<br /> <br /> Every Ventrue descends from an influential and powerful methuselah. That's just how clans, bloodlines, and the embrace works, especially for a lineage-sensitive clan like the Ventrue. That just means she's a Ventrue. She has lots of money and mortal influence? So does every Ventrue, that's kind of how Ventrues work. She &quot;works hard&quot;? so does every other Ventrue.<br /> <br /> None of this adequately explains how she's mysteriously Hardestadt <b>3.0</b>. Especially when her character sheet and modus operandi is basically a laundry list of &quot;everything we said we want to move away from, thematically, with v5&quot; combined with &quot;everything that will get you hunted and killed by the Second Inquisition&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's funny you mention the power vacuum created by the Beckoning. Here's a better question in light of that, why isn't <i>she</i> being Beckoned? She's canonically 8th, vampires of up to 9th are being Beckoned, correlative to but not dependent upon age. She should by all rights be among them, which is yet another area in which this character breaks lore and theme as established by v5.<br /> <br /> No Ventrue in their right mind should be willing to deal with her, let alone line up around the block to answer to her beck and call. She's too high profile, reckless with her contacts and influence if we're to believe what's said about how she wields them contrasted against established v5 fluff, and dealing with her is far too risky with the Second Inquisition around. The way she's written, if she goes down practically the entire clan goes down, and that's a level of centralization with which even the Ventrue would hestitate.<br /> <br /> So, there's only one of two ways I can see this character.<br /> <br /> Either she is, as you said, working with the SI. Or, she's an infiltrator playing at some Kemintiri-level bullshit. Or, it's an alternate identity for a Ventrue elder or methuselah. Or, the clan is setting her up as the ultimate patsy so that whenever she <i>does</i> go down it looks to the SI they've tagged Ventrue Prime, and leave the rest alone. Assuming there's some lore-consistent, interesting, endgame here.<br /> <br /> I gotta admit, it actually would be funny as hell if Savona was Kemintiri.<br /> <br /> But, I fear the second way is probably closer to the truth: the writers ditched Jan for good reason as the Ventrue signature character, but still needed one, so they made #girlboss without general regard for anything else they wrote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T17:38:03-07:00","id":1516844,"title":"","content":"<br /> Not to be rude, Theodrin, but I think you misread Shadeprowler.<br /> <br /> I've looked at Shade's answer twice now and I completely missed any mention of this Savona lady working with the Inquisition. Instead, they mention the SI got their inroads into Cainite society NOT from &quot;their influence of mortal society,&quot; but from the NSA uncovering Schrecknet. Free to correct me if I'm wrong, but I think Shadeprowler's argument was that it was the Ventrue's &quot;influence over mortals&quot; that <i>protected</i> (at least some of) them. And, if my assumption is right, that is a very good argument for getting more involved. Whether the SI is still tied to the Vatican or not, they might think twice of hitting a Vampire if Catholics (or any mortals) could end up as collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Saying &quot;all Ventrue descend from influential and powerful methuselahs&quot; is a bit like saying &quot;all British Royal children are descended from King George the VIth. While technically correct, it totally ignores that Prince George and Prince Louis are considered in line for the Throne, while Archie Harrison is not. If Ventrue need to compete so badly with anyone <i>outside</i> their Clan, what makes you think they'll be any less competitive <i>within</i>? There is no way the Ventrue consider themselves equals<br /> <br /> Another thing Shade mentioned was that pesky Beckoning. For better or worse, almost everyone who was anyone in the Ventrue Inner Circle seems to have buggered off, either because of some mental compulsion, or maybe they heard a rumor Theo Bell was in the area. That creates a power vacuum, which <i>someone</i> is going to fill, whether it's a strangely British sounding man who claimed to have served Napoleon, or, in this case, someone with the body of a sixty year old lady. <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T18:00:35-07:00","id":1516845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1516844#post1516844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've looked at Shade's answer twice now and I completely missed any mention of this Savona lady working with the Inquisition...</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication is the Ventrue &quot;protected&quot; themselves by redirecting the SI towards other clans. Which dovetails into the next point...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Instead, they mention the SI got their inroads into Cainite society NOT from &quot;their influence of mortal society,&quot; but from the NSA uncovering Schrecknet... </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the NSA cracked ShreckNet. They <i>found</i> ShreckNet because the Camarilla was fucking around using the post-9/11 surveillance state to wage the sect war, and started liaising off-the-record with other agencies whose members had <i>already</i> been following breadcrumbs thanks to vampiric shenanigans elsewhere. I'm not just talking about SAD, it had gone so far vampires were even on the CDC's radar via tracing anomalous bloodborne illness outbreaks, and discrepancies in blood supplies and transportation (<i>Hunters Hunted</i>).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> If Ventrue need to compete so badly with anyone <i>outside</i> their Clan, what makes you think they'll be any less competitive <i>within</i>? There is no way the Ventrue consider themselves equals </div> </div> </div>That's rather the point. The way this is all presented, Ventrue are <i>very</i> uncharacteristically rallying of their own volition behind this one ancilla who seems to have just...<i>appeared</i>, lineage be damned. They like to present a unified front only to outsiders; behind closed doors, the situation as of v5 should be all but a free-for-all over clan leadership and hierarchy. And, internally that should be a &quot;all hands on deck&quot; red flag for those not already under her influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Another thing Shade mentioned was that pesky Beckoning.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Yep. And again, she's 8th generation so why isn't <i>she</i> being Beckoned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T18:33:44-07:00","id":1516850,"title":"","content":"<br /> Why hasn't Helena been beckoned? Or Mithras/Monty Coven (depending of how anyone playing the chronicle resolved it)?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but the more I'm in this thread, the more I'm wondering just what the problem Fiorenza Savona <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> Is it because she's a new character? Because that's what happens when a setting is advanced. Old characters are written off, and newer ones are introduced.<br /> <br /> Is it because she's &quot;an ancilla?&quot; Because if she's old enough to be Beckoned, I'd say she's also old enough to count as an Elder.<br /> <br /> Is it because &quot;she's involved in mortal affairs?&quot; Because that's what Ventrue DO. They get involved in mortal institutions, even if it's through proxies in middle management.<br /> <br /> Is it because her artwork shows her as a sixty year old lady? Well, not every Kindred is embraced at the peak of youth. Both the Revised Clanbooks for Ravnos and Giovanni had elderly woman vampires in the character templates. The game is thirty years old; a woman playing Vampire since the beginning would be roughly that age by now. We don't tell <a href=\"https://youtu.be/eqdOdcprq-M\" target=\"_blank\">Dave from Nerdarchy</a> that he's too old to play Dungeons and Dragons, why is an old lady playing Vampire such a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T23:26:46-07:00","id":1516858,"title":"","content":"Indeed, how <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch\">Father Enoch</a> </b>\u200bsaid, I ment the Venture mostly avoided the SI attention because of the mortal influence Savona and others like her built up.<br /> Private Herds, money, influence - just like in the time of the First Inquisition, this time the Ventrue was mostly came out from the ordeal mostly unscathed - but had to a bit reinvent their immage.<br /> They always did this during their history led by &quot;paragon figures&quot;<br /> In the Dark Ages the Ventrue began infiltrating existing government as feudal lords, but mostly were posing as kings and merchant princes, expanded their influence through trade routes and battles, and became a force to be reckoned with.<br /> In the Victorian Ages, the combination of centuries-old feudalism with the <i>nouveau riche</i> middle class served to keep the Ventrue at the top of the power structure, during this time the Ventrue learned to temper their cutthroat business dealings with an outward veneer of philanthropy. They remained, of course, a clan out for profit and prestige.<br /> In the 20-21th century the Clan made massive profits and sinked its tendrils into the growing government bureaucracies that came to dominate industrialized governments.<br /> This time? one of that paragon figures is Savona<br /> Maybe I interpreted it wrong, but the SI mostly avoided the Ventrue while their competition, the Toreador, the Tremere, the Brujah (even with their departure) were hit HARD, loosing age old strongholds and domains - and I think and totally could be wrong -.this was because of the mortal influence Savona and others like her built up.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1516845#post1516845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. And again, she's 8th generation so why isn't <i>she</i> being Beckoned?</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the Beckoning, there is 0 concrete information about it<br /> Kindred of Generations Ninth or lower are compelled to travel to the general area of the Middle East and other regions that supported early human civilization... in theory yet vampires are immune to its siren call for... god know why?<br /> Age? Date of Embrace? Blood bond? Diableire?<br /> Menele went then why Helena stayed?<br /> Besides, 8th is not that high, and Savona as far as I know is not an Elder... many of like her stayed<br /> Why?<br /> Your guess is as good as mine<br /> But the Elder Ventrue, influental and older went - I think - and that left a power vacuum<br /> <br /> If she would be of 10th generation would be easier for you to accept? Then it is just a matter of semantics, could be an anomaly like many other who resisted the call.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T17:57:34-07:00","id":1516934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1516858#post1516858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They always did this during their history led by &quot;paragon figures&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, contrast how Ventrue historically underwent these transitions, against what's said of Savona. Or not to put too fine a point in it, the distinct complete <i>lack</i> of internal strife in any way whatsoever as the new pecking order is established. The last time it occurred, it was so nasty it ended up spawning <i>an entire bloodline</i> so radically opposed to the new regime they developed <i>Auspex</i> for the sole purpose of ferreting out their own clan's conspiracies and machinations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with the Beckoning, there is 0 concrete information about it </div> </div> </div>Yeah there is. Case in point,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Menele went then why Helena stayed? </div> </div> </div>We know <i>exactly</i> how Helena pulled it off. Infernalism was probably a contributing factor to it, but the serial diablerie was the key factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, 8th is not that high... </div> </div> </div>It is actually, but that's neither here nor there. It's one generation <i>lower</i> than the apparent breakpoint for who's being Beckoned, and who isn't, and that's what matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Elder Ventrue, influental and older went - I think - and that left a power vacuum... </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. The Ventrue <i>should</i> be in the middle of an internal power struggle deciding the new pecking order, following their past tendencies. If she were among a handful of Ventrue vying for clan leadership -- Lucinde being one of them, as well as <i>some</i> presumptive heir to Hardestadt, and probably Kevin Jackson as well -- it would be a far more believable scenario. Instead, what we have so far is Savona saying &quot;I'm the captain now&quot;, and basically every other Ventrue up to and including a fucking <i>Alastor</i> turned Justicar saying &quot;yeah, we're cool with that&quot;. And <i>there's</i> the loudass klaxon and flashing red alarm.<br /> <br /> This is, almost line-by-line, a script Lucinde in particular has had to deal with in the past. Especially given the <i>really, amazingly, phenomenally fortuitous </i>timeline for one vampire in particular with whom Lucinde's dealt repeatedly in the past. A vampire who has bad blood with the Setites (whose negotiations to join the Camarilla got sabotaged), a <i>massive</i> grudge against the Tremere (who got, well, exploded), but not nearly as big as the grudge she bears against the Ventrue (who she has a habit of impersonating and infiltrating).<br /> <br /> <i>(Hint: I joked, but she probably actually is Kemintiri to have been able to have made remotely this scale of power play in such a short time.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 07-01-2023, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T18:32:05-07:00","id":1516936,"title":"","content":"Comment deleted because I am just tired and sorry I even responded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 07-01-2023, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T04:00:13-07:00","id":1516960,"title":"","content":"The Beckoning, we know that, is not a &quot;vanish button&quot;, more of a process; when you are of the 8th generation and above, you will start hearing those voices, and they will get the noisier and the stronger the stronger you become; <br /> <br /> A strong Blood Bond can get in the way of the call, as well as the destruction of a strong Blood Bond; diablerie can also stop the process; we also don't know whether the call is uniform or it is influenced by what Methuselas and possibly Antidiluvians are awake, or how the Gehenna War is going; <br /> <br /> So probably Fiorenza is strong enough to get noticed in the Ventrue hierarchy, but not enough that the Beckoning is more than an obsessive afterthought that slowly poisons her days;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T04:03:10-07:00","id":1516961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1516934#post1516934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yeah. The Ventrue <i>should</i> be in the middle of an internal power struggle deciding the new pecking order, following their past tendencies. If she were among a handful of Ventrue vying for clan leadership -- Lucinde being one of them, as well as <i>some</i> presumptive heir to Hardestadt, and probably Kevin Jackson as well -- it would be a far more believable scenario. Instead, what we have so far is Savona saying &quot;I'm the captain now&quot;, and basically every other Ventrue up to and including a fucking <i>Alastor</i> turned Justicar saying &quot;yeah, we're cool with that&quot;. And <i>there's</i> the loudass klaxon and flashing red alarm.[/I]</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading the CAMARILLA sourcebook, I'm actually fairly convinced that Lucinde and the Archons are behind the metamorphosis of the Sect, and the fall of Hardestadt and the fascistisation of the Camarilla are the most visible part of a military coup<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T08:53:52-07:00","id":1517075,"title":"","content":"In regards to the Beckoning subplot. It's quite possible that there antidulivans are being selective to whom they call to there ancient homelands and may want powerful 8th or 9th generation kindred to stay where there at to keep there fiefdoms in capable proven hands instead of unknown neonate or ancilla who maybe unsuited for such tasks. That is how we play it in our game to justify why we have a couple of 9th generation kindred hanging about including one 8th generation elder.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that is why this Ventrue ancilla is still around and not departing for the middle east.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T01:59:16-07:00","id":1517254,"title":"","content":"There isn't a <i>rule</i> for the Beckoning. It's a tool for Storytellers (and authors) to remove the vampires they want gone and keep the ones they want to remain. It's mysterious in-setting, and some vampires find ways around it, but it's not supposed to be a phenomenon that affects every vampire equally, no more than influenza kills everyone who catches it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T08:09:56-07:00","id":1517276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1517254#post1517254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a <i>rule</i> for the Beckoning. It's a tool for Storytellers (and authors) to remove the vampires they want gone and keep the ones they want to remain. It's mysterious in-setting, and some vampires find ways around it, but it's not supposed to be a phenomenon that affects every vampire equally, no more than influenza kills everyone who catches it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the idea that we have in our games that some of the big shots are still around and not feel a need to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T05:52:46-07:00","id":1518925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1517254#post1517254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There isn't a <i>rule</i> for the Beckoning. It's a tool for Storytellers (and authors) to remove the vampires they want gone and keep the ones they want to remain. It's mysterious in-setting, and some vampires find ways around it, but it's not supposed to be a phenomenon that affects every vampire equally, no more than influenza kills everyone who catches it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given you're involvement however in Beckett's Jyhad Diary and the amount of plot threads you helped gather up and provide some measure of resolution you have to unserstand people's distaste for this stance. It's been 5 years since the setting was fundamentally changed by V5 and outside of OPP sourcebooks we have no answers or improvement of the metaplot. Even if a solid answer wasn't provided, but some more what if scenarios were provided, letting GMs decide for their table for this and other head scratchers positioned by V5 it'd be a vast improvement. <br /> <br /> The people who loved VtM did so in partly because of the metaplot, (it is what divided players between VtM and the sandbox of Requiem)and I don't understand why money is being left on the table by Paradox refusing to develop it further. GMs don't have to use it, but there are people who will buy the books just to read the setting updates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T08:27:41-07:00","id":1518934,"title":"","content":"I believe she is a neonate, thats what the wiki implies anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T08:51:47-07:00","id":1518935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1518925#post1518925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given you're involvement however in Beckett's Jyhad Diary and the amount of plot threads you helped gather up and provide some measure of resolution you have to unserstand people's distaste for this stance. It's been 5 years since the setting was fundamentally changed by V5 and outside of OPP sourcebooks we have no answers or improvement of the metaplot. Even if a solid answer wasn't provided, but some more what if scenarios were provided, letting GMs decide for their table for this and other head scratchers positioned by V5 it'd be a vast improvement.<br /> <br /> The people who loved VtM did so in partly because of the metaplot, (it is what divided players between VtM and the sandbox of Requiem)and I don't understand why money is being left on the table by Paradox refusing to develop it further. GMs don't have to use it, but there are people who will buy the books just to read the setting updates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do understand your distaste. It does not however appear to be in V5's current trajectory to provide metaplot mysteries or answers to them. The books that have come out since Forbidden Religions are arguably more metaplot agnostic than V20, in the sense they're not building up grand plots or character arcs, and are leaving each chronicle, player option, and clan as a tool in a kit rather than a piece of the world's fabric. <br /> <br /> Some people will like this (clearly some do, based on the #Vamily popularity, buzz on the Official WoD Discord, etc.) and some won't, yourself included. I have my tastes as well, which I suspect are evident through the books I developed. I'm not writing the TTRPG any more, however, and I don't begrudge Paradox and Renegade taking their own course and appealing to a different market, even though yes, it does upset people who want things to be the other way. Interestingly, there's more metaplot &quot;advancement&quot; in games like Swansong (the video game) and Chapters (the board game), both of which I worked on, than the Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> In terms of your saying &quot;there are people who will buy the books just to read the setting updates&quot;, it is quite possible Paradox and Renegade crunched the numbers and decided that's not a market they want to create books for, especially with the existence of the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> But to all this, don't be disheartened. Even if V5 isn't the game you want it to be right now, there's loads of enthralling material out there and more to come, whether in the World of Darkness or games beyond it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T08:02:03-07:00","id":1519029,"title":"","content":"Appreciate your response as always.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T05:58:44-07:00","id":1519338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1518935#post1518935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But to all this, don't be disheartened. Even if V5 isn't the game you want it to be right now, there's loads of enthralling material out there and more to come, whether in the World of Darkness or games beyond it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That seems intriguing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T08:33:49-07:00","id":1519343,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I don't see the metaplot as having &quot;gone away&quot; so much as localized, with the Beckoning and Second Inquisition having stripped away the globe-spanning operatics. The major cities have their own thing going on as always, and published materials support it just fine. The state of affairs is far more reminiscent of the Dark Ages setting for this, than it is modern nights in past editions -- and that's okay.<br /> <br /> The issue with VtM metaplot, is unless the ST is running something on the scope of Giovanni Chronicles or Transylvania Chronicles, or published chronicles like those of Chicago or New York, the &quot;big picture&quot; just...doesn't matter at all, really. And, chronicles on that scale are near-universally panned for their railroaded, &quot;metaplot theme park&quot; nature, and have to be rebuilt practically from the ground up (or include significant interlude stories) just to introduce the <i>potential</i> for player agency. It's nice to see where the puzzle pieces fit from that perspective, but it's hardly necessary to run a compelling chronicle -- and more often than not, a <i>hindrance</i> depending on how well-versed players are, and their capacity to figure out plot threads and pick nits out-of-character.<br /> <br /> All of this rather shines a spotlight on the Savona anomaly: it hearkens to the &quot;meet the new boss, same as the old boss&quot; nature of vampiric affairs with a sprinkle of the older style of global intrigue, but that itself contradicts with v5's new metaplot direction and theme. And, without a <i>whiff</i> that something else may be going on under the hood to resolve that contradiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T22:56:01-07:00","id":1519396,"title":"","content":"I think the whole probelm would be solved if we would know some concrete information about the Beckoning, namely what it really was/is and how it worked... - and what happened with the beconed really? Even the &quot;well several felt the blood bond snap so probably they died&quot; is a bit... off-note. It could even be the greates trick of them all, the Elders went off the map, but still giggle behind the curtains. Just a few either not recieved the memo or wanted to stay in the spotlight... or were chosen to stay in the spotlight...<br /> But that is just my two cents","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T23:29:17-07:00","id":1519398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1519343#post1519343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I don't see the metaplot as having &quot;gone away&quot; so much as localized, with the Beckoning and Second Inquisition having stripped away the globe-spanning operatics. The major cities have their own thing going on as always, and published materials support it just fine. The state of affairs is far more reminiscent of the Dark Ages setting for this, than it is modern nights in past editions -- and that's okay.<br /> <br /> The issue with VtM metaplot, is unless the ST is running something on the scope of Giovanni Chronicles or Transylvania Chronicles, or published chronicles like those of Chicago or New York, the &quot;big picture&quot; just...doesn't matter at all, really. And, chronicles on that scale are near-universally panned for their railroaded, &quot;metaplot theme park&quot; nature, and have to be rebuilt practically from the ground up (or include significant interlude stories) just to introduce the <i>potential</i> for player agency. It's nice to see where the puzzle pieces fit from that perspective, but it's hardly necessary to run a compelling chronicle -- and more often than not, a <i>hindrance</i> depending on how well-versed players are, and their capacity to figure out plot threads and pick nits out-of-character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that such &quot;big picture&quot; or scope is even kind of questionable in the case of the Giovanni Chronicles at least - Last Supper is a huge event but also pretty much self-contained, Blood &amp; Fire and the Sun Has Set theoretically follow on it, but are all about the PCs as agents of the Camarilla Founders doing a macguffin hunt in their stead while growing into ancillae and elders on their own right with only loose ties to part 1.<br /> <br /> And Nuova Mallatia....well, its writers admit themselves they just did whatever since the original team was utterly gone, nobody knew what they originally planned for a conclusion. Plus the super cop-out move of changing the viewpoint to a branch of the Giovanni (mostly as ghouls) being trampled over by Marianna Giovanni &amp;/or the Conspiracy of Isaac childer.<br /> <br /> Anyway, constant name-dropping and globe-trotting aside, the scope and stakes weren't exactly that huge or clear. Transylvania Chronicles for al its narrative schizophrenia was definitely much more epic in its scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-02T09:23:59-07:00","id":1519447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516788-please-someone-explain-this-fiorenza-savona-thing?p=1518934#post1518934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe she is a neonate, thats what the wiki implies anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought she was a younger Ancilla myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}